<section class="fragment-plan" data-artifact="plan" data-slice="viewer-lineup-tactics" data-rev="2">
  <table class="files-touched pl-files">
    <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Status</th><th>Module</th><th>Lines</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> web/lineup.mjs + tests</summary><div class="pl-card">Lineup legality: eleven starters, a goalkeeper in goal, no player twice, bench within the tactics file's bench size. One reason at a time for the inline message.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>web logic</td><td>+260</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> web/pending.mjs + tests</summary><div class="pl-card">The pending-change list mirrors the engine queue by queue id: Queued, Applies now, Applied, Rejected. Each chip carries its word.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>web logic</td><td>+220</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">ui</span> lineup editor, tactics panel, substitution picker + test</summary><div class="pl-card">Ordinary DOM, keyboard operable, click-to-place first. Rendered from the squads and tactics schema in the opening message. Kick-off sends the lineup, then start.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>web panels</td><td>+690</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">ui</span> web/components/chip.css</summary><div class="pl-card">Chip styles from the token file. Colour never carries the state alone.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>web page</td><td>+60</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">ui</span> web/index.html, web/main.mjs</summary><div class="pl-card">The editor replaces the placeholder. Tactics and substitution region. The pending() and lineup() test readers.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>web page</td><td>+110 / -8</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">contract</span> crates/protocol message.rs, lib.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">Version 3: squads and setup on each team, the tactics schema and substitution limit in the opening message, the lineup command, and a typed change detail.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>protocol</td><td>+170 / -5</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">service</span> crates/stream control.rs, lib.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">Pre-match hold, lineup check and storage, and a change inbox that carries the acknowledged identifier.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>stream</td><td>+142 / -6</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine sim.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">A page-chosen lineup and bench replace the pre-match setup before the match is built.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>engine</td><td>+40</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">cli</span> engine-cli hello.rs (new), serve, stream driver, record, bench</summary><div class="pl-card">One opening-message builder. Serve holds until start. The driver drains the inbox while running and maps engine identifiers back to socket identifiers.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>engine-cli</td><td>+217 / -60</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">docs</span> protocol reference and stream tests</summary><div class="pl-card">Version 3 sections and the detail shapes. Test team literals gain the new fields.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>docs, tests</td><td>+78 / -5</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="pl-risks">
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>Two queues number one change differently.</strong> The socket queue and the engine queue each assign an identifier. The driver maps one to the other, and a test asserts that the applied event carries the acknowledged identifier.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>The pre-match hold changes every served match.</strong> Only the served session holds. Recording, benchmarking, and resuming keep producing at once.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><strong>Version 3 refuses older recordings.</strong> No recording is committed. Tests record fresh ones.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><strong>Shared opening-message builder with the match-day panels.</strong> Extend whichever builder lands first, and raise the version only once.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><strong>A change made while paused must wait for the next dead ball.</strong> The inbox drains only while the match runs. A driver test covers it.</aside>
  </div>

  <details class="pl-revs"><summary>2 prior revisions</summary><ul><li><a href="history/04-plan-viewer-lineup-tactics-0.md">rev 0</a>: first plan, contract-independent half, two open questions.</li><li><a href="history/04-plan-viewer-lineup-tactics-1.md">rev 1</a>: auto-review, seven drifts fixed, questions still open.</li></ul></details>

